.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include \(dqbashclient.h\(dq

bc_client_t *bc_connect_named_pipe(const char *pipe_name);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Establishes a connection to a running \f[CR]bash\-server(1)\f[R]
instance through a Windows Named Pipe.
This transport is available only on Cygwin and provides an alternative
to Unix domain sockets for inter\-process communication on Windows.
.PP
The \f[CR]pipe_name\f[R] parameter specifies the Named Pipe path, which
must follow the Windows Named Pipe naming convention:
.IP
.EX
\(rs\(rs.\(rspipe\(rs<name>
.EE
.PP
On Cygwin, this is typically written as:
.IP
.EX
//./pipe/<name>
.EE
.PP
If \f[CR]pipe_name\f[R] is NULL, the function attempts to resolve the
pipe name from the server configuration using the standard search order
(see \f[CR]bc_connect(3)\f[R] for details).
.PP
The Named Pipe connection uses the server\(cqs DACL security descriptor
for access control.
The calling process must have permission to open the pipe for read/write
access.
.PP
After a successful connection, the caller must authenticate with
\f[CR]bc_auth(3)\f[R] before issuing any commands.
